From 962d63128a209631c9c1221d24084db550ea05a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:34:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): dead-watcher alert review fixes - running loop,
 incident key, backoff, hub host [daveey]

Review of #3751 at 8c1dc18f49bc (REQUEST_CHANGES):
- No card while a sync loop runs now: this process's kanban_sync_claims._STATE.loop
  (dispatcher and watcher share the gateway process), else a live .sync.lock holder.
  A respawned loop keeps the old crash record until its first round completes.
- Incident = the alert's own first_seen_dead (the first crash record's since), kept
  across crash/respawn cycles whatever the crash text; a cleared record ends it.
- A failed tasks/create-task/comment call records last_attempt/last_error and waits
  10 min. _updating() moved after the cheap record read.
- The hub gateway never files through the courier (its card would wait on its own
  sync-gated board): one ERROR per incident plus hub_incident in the state file.
  Known gap: the hub's own dead sync needs a non-Kanban route.
- Host label is ident.gateway, as the SchemaAhead alarm uses.
- 5-minute test asserts the exact tasks/create-task argv and that
  kanban_db.create_task (the local outbox path) is not called.

Tests: test_kanban_sync_watcher_alert 15 passed; mutation (running-loop guard and
backoff disabled) fails 4 of them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
